<problem>
    <title>Challenge Problem</title>
    <statement>
        <p>
            Consider the solid of revolution around the <m>x</m>-axis of the curve <m>y=f(x)</m>
            over the interval <m>x\in[a,b]</m>. Explain the following formula for the surface area of
            this solid:
            <m>S \ =\ \int_a^b 2\pi f(x)\sqrt{1{+}(f'(x))^2\,}\, dx\,.</m>
            <hint>
                <p>
                    <m>
                        \sqrt{(\Delta x)^2 + (\Delta y)^2\,}
                        \ =\ \sqrt{1+(\frac{\Delta y}{\Delta x})^2\,}\ \Delta x
                        \ \approx\ \sqrt{1+(\frac{dy}{dx})^2\, }\ \Delta x
                    </m>.
                </p>
            </hint>
        </p>

    </statement>
    <solution>
        <p>
            
        </p>
    </solution>
</problem>

